from pathlib import Path
import json
# All code and copy below are production content; spreadsheet cells are topic data.
D={
2: ('Tags describe the role of content on a web page.','<p>Hello, web!</p>','<p>Hello, web!</p>','Most elements have an opening tag, content, and a closing tag.','A slash marks the closing tag.','Void elements, like images, have no closing tag in HTML.','Write a paragraph element containing your name.'),
3: ('Headings organize a page into meaningful sections.','<h1>My blog</h1>\n<h2>Latest posts</h2>','<h1>My blog</h1><h2>Latest posts</h2>','H one is the highest heading level; H six is the lowest.','Use heading levels to describe the hierarchy of your content.','Choose headings for meaning, rather than just their default size.','Create a page title and a heading for its first section.'),
4: ('A paragraph element groups a piece of text into a paragraph.','<p>Hello, web!</p>\n<p>Keep learning.</p>','<p>Hello, web!</p><p>Keep learning.</p>','Wrap each paragraph in opening and closing P tags.','Browsers normally leave space between paragraphs.','Extra spaces and line breaks in source code usually collapse.','Write two paragraphs about something you enjoy.'),
5: ('Links connect your page to other pages or resources.','<a href="https://example.com">\n  Visit Example\n</a>','<a href="https://example.com">Visit Example</a>','The anchor element creates the link; H ref supplies its destination.','The text between the tags becomes the clickable label.','Use descriptive link text so people know where they are going.','Add a link to a website you find useful.'),
6: ('An image element embeds a picture in your page.','<img src="cat.jpg"\n     alt="An orange cat">','<div style="font-size:120px">🐈</div><p>An orange cat</p>','Source identifies the image file; alt provides a text alternative.','Describe useful image content in the alternative text.','The image element is void, so it has no closing tag.','Add a local image with a useful text description.'),
7: ('Lists group related items in a meaningful order.','<ul>\n  <li>HTML</li>\n  <li>CSS</li>\n</ul>','<ul><li>HTML</li><li>CSS</li></ul>','Use an unordered list for bullets, and an ordered list for numbering.','Each list item belongs inside an L I element.','Pick numbering when the sequence of the items matters.','Create a numbered list of three steps in your morning routine.'),
8: ('A button is a control that people can activate.','<button type="button">\n  Say hello\n</button>','<button>Say hello</button>','Use the button element to create an accessible native control.','JavaScript can listen for a click and perform an action.','Inside a form, specify the type to avoid accidental submission.','Create a button with a clear action label.'),
9: ('Attributes provide additional information about an element.','<p id="intro" class="note">\n  Welcome!\n</p>','<p style="background:#d7f8e6;padding:20px">Welcome!</p>','Write attributes inside the opening tag, commonly as name and value.','An I D identifies one element; a class can group several.','Keep each I D unique within the document.','Give two paragraphs the same class and different identifiers.'),
10: ('Div and span are generic containers for grouping content.','<div>\n  A <span>special</span> word\n</div>','<div>A <span style="background:#ffcc99">special</span> word</div>','A div is block level by default; a span is inline.','Use a span to group words within a line of text.','Prefer a meaningful semantic element when one fits your content.','Wrap a sentence in a div and one word in a span.'),
11: ('HTML comments are notes that browsers do not display as page content.','<!-- Main heading -->\n<h1>Hello!</h1>','<h1>Hello!</h1>','A comment begins with an angle bracket, exclamation mark, and two hyphens.','It ends with two hyphens and a closing angle bracket.','Comments remain visible in source code, so never put secrets there.','Add a short comment explaining the next section of your page.'),
12: ('Line breaks and thematic breaks have different meanings.','<p>Line one<br>Line two</p>\n<hr>\n<p>A new section</p>','<p>Line one<br>Line two</p><hr><p>A new section</p>','B R creates a line break; H R marks a thematic break.','A line break suits addresses and lines of a poem.','Use C S S spacing instead of repeated break elements for layout.','Write a two-line address, then add a thematic break below it.'),
13: ('Tables organize data into rows and columns.','<table>\n <tr><th>Skill</th></tr>\n <tr><td>HTML</td></tr>\n</table>','<table border="1" cellpadding="16"><tr><th>Skill</th></tr><tr><td>HTML</td></tr></table>','T R defines a row, T H a header, and T D a cell.','A caption can describe what the table contains.','Use tables for data, rather than for arranging an entire page.','Create a table showing two skills and their practice time.'),
14: ('A form groups controls that collect information from a user.','<form>\n <label>Email\n  <input type="email"\n         name="email">\n </label>\n <button>Send</button>\n</form>','<label>Email <input placeholder="you@example.com"></label><p><button>Send</button></p>','Give controls labels so people can understand what to enter.','The name attribute identifies a field when form data is submitted.','A form alone does not save data; it needs a submission handler.','Create a labeled email field and a submit button.'),
15: ('Input types tell a browser what kind of value to collect.','<input type="email">\n<input type="password">\n<input type="number">','<p><input placeholder="Email"></p><p><input type="password" value="example"></p><p><input type="number" value="3"></p>','Email, password, and number types offer different input behavior.','An email field can participate in browser validation.','Masking a password field does not encrypt or securely store its value.','Try three input types and compare their behavior.'),
16: ('Checkboxes allow independent choices; radio buttons select within a group.','<input type="checkbox"> CSS\n<input type="radio"\n       name="level"> Beginner','<p><input type="checkbox" checked> HTML</p><p><input type="checkbox" checked> CSS</p><p><input type="radio" checked> Beginner</p>','Use the same name for radio buttons that belong to one group.','Checkboxes are useful when several options may be selected together.','Associate every control with a label, including checkboxes and radios.','Create two skill checkboxes and a radio group for experience level.'),
17: ('A select element presents a list of choices.','<label>Level\n <select name="level">\n  <option>Beginner</option>\n  <option>Intermediate</option>\n </select>\n</label>','<label>Level <select><option>Beginner</option><option>Intermediate</option></select></label>','Each option inside the select becomes one available choice.','A value attribute can specify the data submitted for an option.','Use a label so the purpose of the selection is clear.','Create a dropdown with three learning goals.'),
18: ('Semantic HTML describes the purpose of your content.','<header>My site</header>\n<nav>Home | About</nav>\n<main>Latest lesson</main>\n<footer>Contact</footer>','<header><h2>My site</h2></header><nav>Home | About</nav><main><p>Latest lesson</p></main><footer>Contact</footer>','Header, navigation, main, and footer give sections meaningful roles.','These landmarks help assistive technology users navigate a page.','Choose elements by meaning, rather than their appearance.','Replace generic page containers with suitable semantic elements.'),
19: ('HTML can embed sound and video with native playback controls.','<video controls\n       src="lesson.mp4">\n Your browser needs video support.\n</video>','<div style="background:#14213b;color:white;padding:50px;text-align:center">▶<p>lesson.mp4</p></div>','Use audio for sound and video for moving pictures.','The controls attribute adds the browser playback interface.','Add captions for spoken video content, and avoid relying on autoplay.','Embed a local video and show its playback controls.'),
20: ('Document metadata describes a page to browsers and other services.','<head>\n <title>My first site</title>\n <meta name="viewport"\n content="width=device-width,\n initial-scale=1">\n</head>','<div style="background:#dde4ee;padding:18px">◉ My first site</div><h2>Page content</h2>','The title element supplies the browser tab title.','The viewport meta tag supports appropriate sizing on mobile screens.','Metadata belongs in the head; visible page content belongs in the body.','Add a useful title and a viewport declaration to your document.'),
21: ('C S S controls how your HTML content looks.','p {\n  color: purple;\n  font-size: 24px;\n}','<p style="color:purple;font-size:42px">Hello, style!</p>','A rule combines a selector with declarations inside braces.','Each declaration pairs a property with a value.','Keep the content meaningful even before its styling loads.','Change a paragraph color and font size.'),
22: ('You can add C S S inline, inside a document, or in a separate file.','<!-- In the document head -->\n<link rel="stylesheet"\n      href="styles.css">','<p style="color:#6141b7">One stylesheet.</p><p style="color:#6141b7">Many matching elements.</p>','Inline styles use an attribute; internal styles use a style element.','An external stylesheet can be shared across several pages.','Keep larger projects organized with a separate stylesheet.','Create a styles file and connect it to your HTML document.'),
23: ('C S S colors can be written as names, hexadecimal values, or color functions.','h1 { color: tomato; }\np { color: #334155; }\na { color: rgb(0 90 200); }','<h2 style="color:tomato">Tomato</h2><p style="color:#334155">Slate</p><a style="color:rgb(0 90 200)">Blue</a>','Different color formats can describe the same visible color.','Choose text and background colors that remain easy to read.','Color alone should not be the only way to communicate meaning.','Style a heading, paragraph, and link using three color formats.'),
24: ('Text properties control the presentation of written content.','h1 {\n font-size: 2rem;\n font-weight: 700;\n letter-spacing: .03em;\n text-align: center;\n}','<h2 style="text-align:center;letter-spacing:4px">HELLO</h2><p style="line-height:1.6">Readable text starts with good spacing.</p>','Font size, weight, and line height affect readability.','Relative units can help text scale with user preferences.','Use real heading elements for structure, even when styling changes their size.','Give a heading bold weight and a paragraph comfortable line spacing.'),
25: ('Background properties paint the area behind an element.','.card {\n background: linear-gradient(\n   135deg, #ffd6a5, #caffbf\n );\n}','<div style="padding:70px 30px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ffd6a5,#caffbf);border-radius:20px">Hello, gradient!</div>','Start with a solid color, or combine colors in a gradient.','A background image can be sized and positioned separately.','Keep foreground text readable across the entire background.','Give a card a two-color gradient background.'),
26: ('The box model describes the space occupied by an element.','.card {\n margin: 16px;\n padding: 24px;\n border: 2px solid teal;\n}','<div style="background:#f6cea2;padding:25px"><div style="border:6px solid teal;padding:30px;background:#d7f5e3">Content</div></div>','From inside out, it has content, padding, border, and margin.','Padding is inside the border; margin is outside it.','With border box sizing, declared width includes padding and borders.','Give a card padding, a border, and outside margin.'),
27: ('Classes and identifiers let C S S select particular elements.','.note { color: teal; }\n#intro { font-weight: 700; }','<p style="color:teal;font-weight:700">Welcome!</p><p style="color:teal">Another note.</p>','A dot selects a class; a hash selects an identifier.','Reuse a class to apply the same style to several elements.','Keep identifiers unique, and avoid unnecessary selector specificity.','Style two elements with one shared class.'),
28: ('Display controls how an element participates in layout.','.tag { display: inline-block; }\n.panel { display: block; }','<div style="background:#d9e8ff;padding:16px">Block</div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:18px;background:#ffd6a5;margin-top:15px">Inline block</span>','Block elements normally start a new line; inline elements flow with text.','Inline block boxes flow inline while accepting width and height.','Display none removes an element from layout and the accessibility tree.','Compare a block container with two inline block labels.'),
29: ('Flexbox arranges items along one main axis.','.row {\n display: flex;\n gap: 12px;\n justify-content: center;\n align-items: center;\n}','<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;justify-content:center"><b style="padding:20px;background:#ffd6a5">1</b><b style="padding:20px;background:#caffbf">2</b><b style="padding:20px;background:#a0c4ff">3</b></div>','Turn the parent into a flex container to arrange its children.','Justify content controls the main axis; align items controls the cross axis.','Those axes change when the flex direction changes.','Center three items in a row with an even gap.'),
30: ('Grid arranges items in rows and columns.','.grid {\n display: grid;\n grid-template-columns:\n   repeat(2, 1fr);\n gap: 12px;\n}','<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:15px">'+''.join('<div style="background:#d9e8ff;padding:25px">'+str(i)+'</div>' for i in range(1,5))+'</div>','Define columns on the parent and place items inside it.','A fractional unit shares available space between grid tracks.','Use grid for layouts that need coordinated rows and columns.','Create a two-column gallery with four cards.'),
31: ('Position changes how an element is placed in a layout.','.card { position: relative; }\n.badge {\n position: absolute;\n top: 8px;\n right: 8px;\n}','<div style="position:relative;background:#d9e8ff;padding:70px 25px">Card<span style="position:absolute;top:12px;right:12px;background:#ffd6a5;padding:10px">New</span></div>','Relative positioning can establish a containing block for an absolute child.','Fixed positioning usually anchors to the viewport; sticky follows a scroll threshold.','Absolute elements leave normal flow, so reserve space when needed.','Place a small badge in the corner of a card.'),
32: ('The hover selector styles an element while a pointer rests over it.','button {\n transition: background .2s;\n}\nbutton:hover {\n background: coral;\n}','<button style="background:coral;color:#182338;padding:25px 45px">Hover state</button>','Combine a hover rule with a transition for a smooth change.','Focus visible can provide a matching cue for keyboard users.','Hover is not reliable on touchscreens; keep essential actions accessible.','Add hover and keyboard focus styles to one button.'),
33: ('Borders define edges, while shadows can suggest depth.','.card {\n border: 2px solid teal;\n border-radius: 16px;\n box-shadow: 0 8px 20px #0002;\n}','<div style="border:3px solid teal;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 12px 25px #0003;padding:55px 25px">A simple card</div>','A border has a width, style, and color.','Border radius rounds the corners; box shadow paints a shadow.','Keep shadows subtle enough that text and boundaries remain clear.','Create a rounded card with a border and soft shadow.'),
34: ('Responsive design adapts a page to different screen sizes.','.cards {\n display: grid;\n grid-template-columns:\n  repeat(auto-fit,\n   minmax(200px, 1fr));\n}','<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:15px"><div style="background:#d9e8ff;padding:25px">Card 1</div><div style="background:#ffd6a5;padding:25px">Card 2</div></div>','Use flexible layouts so content can rearrange as space changes.','Responsive images and a viewport declaration support mobile layouts.','Test real content at narrow widths instead of targeting only one device.','Make a card layout that works on a phone and desktop.'),
35: ('Media queries apply styles when specified conditions match.','.cards { display: block; }\n@media (min-width: 700px) {\n .cards { display: flex; }\n}','<div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><div style="padding:25px;background:#d9e8ff">Wide</div><div style="padding:25px;background:#ffd6a5">Layout</div></div>','A minimum width query can add a wider layout when space is available.','Write the narrow layout first, then add larger-screen adjustments.','Choose breakpoints where the content needs them, rather than by device names.','Stack two cards on mobile and place them together on wider screens.'),
36: ('Transitions and keyframes create changes over time.','@keyframes rise {\n from { opacity: 0;\n        transform: translateY(20px); }\n to   { opacity: 1;\n        transform: translateY(0); }\n}','<div style="background:#d9e8ff;padding:50px 25px;border-radius:16px">↑ Fade and rise</div>','A transition responds to a changed property; keyframes define an animation sequence.','Opacity and transform are useful properties for simple interface motion.','Respect reduced motion preferences and avoid unnecessary movement.','Animate a card entrance with a short fade and upward movement.'),
37: ('JavaScript adds logic and interactive behavior to web pages.','const button =\n document.querySelector("button");\nbutton.addEventListener("click",\n () => alert("Hello!"));','<button>Say hello</button><p style="background:#d7f5e3;padding:20px">Hello!</p>','A script can respond when a user activates a button.','Use JavaScript to update content, validate input, or manage application state.','Keep HTML structure and accessible controls in place before adding behavior.','Make a button respond with a greeting.'),
38: ('Variables give names to values used by your program.','let score = 0;\nscore = score + 1;\nconst player = "Alex";','<h2>Alex</h2><p>Score: <strong>1</strong></p>','Use let when you need to reassign a variable.','Use const when the binding should not be reassigned.','Const does not make the contents of an object immutable.','Store your name and a score, then increase the score.'),
39: ('JavaScript values have different types with different behavior.','const name = "Alex";\nconst score = 10;\nconst ready = true;','<p>“Alex” → string</p><p>10 → number</p><p>true → boolean</p>','Text is a string, a numeric value is a number, and true is a boolean.','The type of operator can help inspect the type of a value.','A number inside quotation marks is a string, which changes some operations.','Create a string, a number, and a boolean.'),
40: ('Operators perform actions such as arithmetic and comparisons.','const total = 5 + 3;\nconst equal = 5 === 5;\nconst larger = 8 > 3;','<h2>5 + 3 = 8</h2><p>5 === 5 → true</p><p>8 > 3 → true</p>','Plus can add numbers, and comparison operators return boolean results.','Strict equality compares values without converting their types.','Plus can also join strings, so check the types of your inputs.','Calculate a total and compare it with a target value.'),
41: ('A function groups instructions into a reusable operation.','function greet(name) {\n return "Hello, " + name;\n}\ngreet("Alex");','<h2>Hello, Alex</h2>','Parameters receive input, and return sends a result back to the caller.','Call the function with an argument to run its instructions.','Returning a value and displaying a value are different actions.','Write a function that returns the sum of two numbers.'),
42: ('If and else let a program choose between actions.','const score = 80;\nif (score >= 50) {\n console.log("Pass");\n} else {\n console.log("Try again");\n}','<h2>Score: 80</h2><p style="color:teal">Pass ✓</p>','The if branch runs when its condition is truthy.','The else branch handles the alternative when that condition is false.','Use comparison operators in conditions, rather than accidental assignment.','Display a different message depending on a practice score.'),
43: ('Loops repeat instructions without writing the same code repeatedly.','for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {\n console.log(i);\n}','<p>1</p><p>2</p><p>3</p>','A for loop can initialize a counter, check a condition, and update it.','Each pass through the loop is called an iteration.','Make sure the condition can become false to avoid an infinite loop.','Print the numbers from one through five with a loop.'),
44: ('An array stores an ordered collection of values.','const skills = ["HTML", "CSS"];\nskills.push("JavaScript");\nconsole.log(skills[0]);','<p>0 → HTML</p><p>1 → CSS</p><p>2 → JavaScript</p>','Array positions start at zero, so index zero gives the first item.','Push appends an item, and length reports the number of items.','An array with three items has a last index of two.','Create an array of three skills and read its first item.'),
45: ('Objects organize information as named properties and their values.','const learner = {\n name: "Alex",\n skill: "HTML"\n};\nconsole.log(learner.name);','<h2>Alex</h2><p>Skill: HTML</p>','Use a property name to access one piece of an object.','Dot notation works with ordinary identifier-style property names.','Use bracket notation when a property name comes from a variable.','Create an object describing a learner and read its name.'),
46: ('The document object model represents a page as objects JavaScript can change.','const heading =\n document.querySelector("h1");\nheading.textContent = "Hello, DOM!";','<h1>Hello, DOM!</h1>','Select an element, then change its text content.','Event listeners can trigger these updates when a user takes an action.','Ensure the element exists before using it, and prefer text content for plain text.','Change a heading when someone presses a button.'),
47: ('A profile card combines meaningful content with a small reusable layout.','<article class="card">\n <h2>Alex</h2>\n <p>Learning web development</p>\n</article>','<article style="padding:35px;border:2px solid teal;border-radius:20px;text-align:center"><div style="font-size:70px">👋</div><h2>Alex</h2><p>Learning web development</p></article>','Start with an article, a heading, and a short introduction.','Add padding, a border, and consistent spacing in your stylesheet.','If you include a portrait, give it appropriate alternative text.','Build a card with your name, a short bio, and one useful link.'),
48: ('A responsive navigation bar keeps important links usable at different widths.','nav {\n display: flex;\n flex-wrap: wrap;\n gap: 16px;\n}','<nav style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;background:#d9e8ff;padding:30px"><a>Home</a><a>About</a><a>Contact</a></nav>','Put navigation links inside a navigation element.','Flex wrapping lets links move to another line when space is tight.','A collapsible menu needs keyboard support and an accessible toggle button.','Build three navigation links that wrap on a narrow screen.'),
49: ('A counter connects application state to visible output.','let count = 0;\nbutton.addEventListener("click",\n () => {\n  count++;\n  output.textContent = count;\n });','<div style="text-align:center"><h1>1</h1><button>−</button> <button>Reset</button> <button>+</button></div>','Store the count in a variable, and update it when a button is pressed.','After every change, update the text shown on the page.','Select the button and output elements before attaching event listeners.','Build plus, minus, and reset controls for your counter.'),
50: ('A to-do list turns user input into items that can be managed.','const item =\n document.createElement("li");\nitem.textContent = input.value;\nlist.append(item);\ninput.value = "";','<h2>Today</h2><p><input placeholder="New task"> <button>Add</button></p><ul><li>Practice HTML</li><li>Learn CSS</li></ul>','Create a list item, assign its text, then append it to the list.','Add a remove control for each task and clear the input after adding.','Reject empty input, and use text content when displaying user-entered text.','Build an add button, a task list, and a remove action.'),
51: ('GitHub Pages can publish a static website from a repository.','my-website/\n  index.html\n  styles.css\n  script.js','<div style="background:#d7f5e3;padding:30px">✓ Your site is live</div><h2>Hello, web!</h2>','Add your static files to a repository and configure Pages in its settings.','For a simple branch deployment, select the source branch and folder.','Pages serves static files; it does not run a custom application server.','Publish a small site, then open its Pages address on your phone.')
}
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
queue=json.loads((root/'queue.json').read_text())
out=[]
for row in queue:
 n=row['videoNumber'];definition,code,preview,rule,tip,caution,exercise=D[n]
 out.append(dict(**row,definition=definition,code=code,preview=preview,rule=rule,tip=tip,caution=caution,exercise=exercise))
(root/'catalog.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
print('Wrote',len(out),'topic-specific video scripts and examples.')
